---
// [CONFIRM] Review this notice, and update it if you add forms, cookies or new tools.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const contactEmail = 'chris@christopher-kelly.co.uk';
---
<Base title="Privacy | Christopher Kelly" description="How christopher-kelly.co.uk handles personal data and cookies." active="home">
  <section class="sec bg-white" data-hero style="border-top:0">
    <div class="wrap-760" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.1rem;line-height:1.75">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="h1">Privacy notice</h1>
      <p>This site is operated by {site.company.legalName}, registered in England and Wales, company number {site.company.number}. {site.company.legalName} is the data controller for personal data collected through this site.</p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-top:1rem">What This Site Collects</h2>
      <p><strong>Visit statistics.</strong> Every visit is counted with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which does not use cookies, does not build a profile of you and does not track you across other sites.</p>
      <p><strong>Product analytics, only with your consent.</strong> If you click Accept on the cookie banner, the site loads PostHog, hosted in the EU. PostHog records the pages you view, the links and buttons you click, and may record a replay of how you used a page, with anything typed into forms masked. I use this to understand which content is useful and to improve the site. If you click Reject, or do nothing, PostHog is not loaded and sets nothing.</p>
      <p><strong>Booking a call.</strong> Booking buttons open my calendar on TidyCal, which collects your name, email address and anything you choose to tell me. I use it only to arrange and prepare for the call. TidyCal processes that data under its own privacy policy.</p>
      <p><strong>Email.</strong> If you email me at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>, the message is routed by Cloudflare to my mailbox, and my replies are sent through Brevo. I keep the correspondence for as long as it's needed to deal with your enquiry and any work that follows.</p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-top:1rem">Cookies And Similar Storage</h2>
      <div style="overflow-x:auto">
        <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.9rem">
          <thead>
            <tr style="text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hair)">
              <th style="padding:.6rem .5rem">Name</th><th style="padding:.6rem .5rem">Set by</th><th style="padding:.6rem .5rem">Purpose</th><th style="padding:.6rem .5rem">Kept for</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--hair)">
              <td style="padding:.6rem .5rem"><code>ck-consent-v1</code> (browser storage)</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem">This site</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem">Remembers whether you accepted or rejected analytics cookies. Strictly necessary.</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem">Until you clear it</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--hair)">
              <td style="padding:.6rem .5rem"><code>ph_*_posthog</code> (cookie and browser storage)</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem">PostHog</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem">Recognises your browser between pages and visits for analytics. Only set after you accept.</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem">Up to 1 year</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>You can change your mind at any time with the <button type="button" data-consent-open style="background:none;border:0;padding:0;font:inherit;color:var(--indigo);text-decoration:underline;cursor:pointer">cookie settings</button> link, which is also in the footer of every page. Rejecting after accepting stops PostHog and removes its cookies from this site.</p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-top:1rem">Your Rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK GDPR you can ask to see, correct or delete the personal data I hold about you, or object to how it's used. Contact me at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. If you're unhappy with the response, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).</p>
      <p class="note">Last updated: 24 October 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
